<section class="research-framework" aria-labelledby="research-focus-heading">
  <h2 id="research-focus-heading">Research Focus</h2>
  <p class="research-intro">
    I bring economic models and computational methods together to study decision-making, interaction, and games among LLM-based agents.
  </p>

  <div class="research-foundations">
    <section class="research-foundation" aria-labelledby="economics-foundation-heading">
      <h3 id="economics-foundation-heading">Economics &amp; Finance</h3>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Game theory</dt>
          <dd>Strategic choices and equilibria</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Utility functions</dt>
          <dd>Preferences, payoffs, and trade-offs</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Information asymmetry</dt>
          <dd>Private information, beliefs, and signals</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Incentive mechanisms</dt>
          <dd>Rules, contracts, and reward design</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section class="research-foundation" aria-labelledby="computing-foundation-heading">
      <h3 id="computing-foundation-heading">Computer Science</h3>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Large language models</dt>
          <dd>Reasoning, communication, and tool use</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Multi-agent systems</dt>
          <dd>Agent architectures and interaction protocols</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Reinforcement learning</dt>
          <dd>Learning policies from rewards and feedback</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Algorithms</dt>
          <dd>Search, planning, and optimisation</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="research-merge" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>

  <div class="research-core">
    <h3>Agentic Economics</h3>
    <p>Agent decision-making, interaction, and strategic behaviour in economic environments.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="research-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="research-areas">
    <section class="research-area" aria-labelledby="agent-negotiation-heading">
      <h4 id="agent-negotiation-heading">Agent Negotiation</h4>
      <p class="research-question">How do LLM agents bargain and reach agreements when preferences and information differ?</p>
      <p class="research-topics"><strong>Focus:</strong> Bargaining &middot; Information asymmetry &middot; Strategic communication</p>
    </section>
    <section class="research-area" aria-labelledby="agent-loyalty-heading">
      <h4 id="agent-loyalty-heading">Agent Loyalty</h4>
      <p class="research-question">When do LLM agents preserve a principal's objectives under conflicting incentives and asymmetric information?</p>
      <p class="research-topics"><strong>Focus:</strong> Principal–agent problems &middot; Incentive compatibility &middot; Delegated objectives</p>
    </section>
    <section class="research-area" aria-labelledby="agent-swarm-heading">
      <h4 id="agent-swarm-heading">Agent Swarm</h4>
      <p class="research-question">
        How do local interactions among many LLM agents produce collective coordination, emergent behaviour, or instability?
      </p>
      <p class="research-topics"><strong>Focus:</strong> Collective coordination &middot; Emergent behaviour &middot; Learning dynamics</p>
    </section>
    <section class="research-area" aria-labelledby="agent-markets-heading">
      <h4 id="agent-markets-heading">Agent Markets</h4>
      <p class="research-question">How do market rules and incentives shape resource allocation, competition, and equilibrium among LLM agents?</p>
      <p class="research-topics"><strong>Focus:</strong> Mechanism design &middot; Resource allocation &middot; Equilibrium</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
